# Mockito's default (inline) mock maker self-attaches a Java agent to the running
# JVM, which fails in sandboxed/CI environments that forbid spawning the external
# attach process ("Could not self-attach to current VM").
#
# The subclass maker needs no agent. Ceiling: it cannot mock final classes, final
# methods, or statics. If a future test needs those, delete this file and add
# -javaagent:<byte-buddy-agent.jar> to the surefire argLine instead.
mock-maker-subclass
